the outside may be gray and drab but  inside the colorful world of football  comes to the fore the museum has spread  over three floors of a former Bank in  downtown Zurich for triode founder and  exhibition designer Lutz Engel curve the  challenge was to convey the powerful  emotions linked to football within the  rigid walls of a static museum through  media as you saw downstairs in the foyer  we have an almost 240 degree wall of  screens on the one side then we've  frozen football in time with individual  objects the museum is a mix of  acceleration and deceleration at the  center of the museum is a rainbow of  football jerseys from all 209 member  associations of FIFA complete with video  content for each shirt  the original FIFA World Cup trophy  stands in pride of place the new museum  accentuates the positive firstly we want  people to have fun secondly we want them  to realize that FIFA is about more than  the scandal of recent years all this has  grown up over 50 60 70 years without the  FIFA rules world football wouldn't exist  and we want to show how a ball can  promote understanding between people  FIFA hopes the new museum will help keep  that ball rolling berlin-based riad has  created a modern museum space that  celebrates the emotion of the beautiful  game  you
 

